<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116205" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμο-θετέω</span></b> , in sacrificing, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>place the raw pieces</i> duly on
			the altar, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.461
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.424
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.458
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμοθετεῖτο, πάντων ἀρχόμενος μελέων,
					ἐς πίονα δημόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.427
				</span></i>
			: later, gerlerally, <i>sacrifice,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρνειόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.1033
				</span></i>
			 (
				Act.
			). (Fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμός,</span>
			<i>raw.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i>, however, says (<i><span class="en">
				134.35
			</span></i>) that some derived it fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦμος</span>
			<i>shoulder,</i> and expld. it accordingly.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
